{
  "slug": "notify",
  "name": "Notify",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "System notifications for Claude Code. Get notified when tasks complete, Claude needs your input, or subagents finish work.\nSupports macOS (terminal-notifier) and Linux (notify-send). Features include:\n- Contextual messages extracted from Claude's actual response\n- Repo and branch context in notification subtitles\n- Duration filtering to suppress notifications for fast responses\n- Per-event customization (sound, app activation, enable/disable)\n- Global or per-project install scopes\n- Interactive setup wizard with editor auto-detection",
  "longDescription": "Ships **4 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (4): `check` (Health check for notify — verifies terminal-notifier/notify-send installed, notify.sh script exists, hook entries in settings.json, and notify-config.json), `setup` (Use only when the user explicitly invokes /notify:setup — one-time setup of cross-platform desktop notifications (installs the notifier,…), `uninstall` (Use only when the user explicitly invokes /notify:uninstall — removes notify's hooks and config while leaving other settings…), `wizard` (Interactive Q&A for customizing notification preferences (sounds, durations, matcher regex, per-event toggles))\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install notify@claude-community` from `ApurvBazari/claude-plugins` (`notify`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "skill",
  "sourceType": "community",
